---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { profile, education, experience, skills, coursework } from '../data/profile';
---
<Layout title="Resume" description="Akaash Bella’s HTML resume: Oregon State education, graduate research, teaching, software engineering projects, technical skills, coursework, and awards.">
  <article class="resume wrap">
    <header class="resume-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / Professional record</p><h1>Akaash Bella</h1><p>Computer science graduate researcher · Portland, Oregon</p><div class="resume-contact"><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a><a href={profile.github}>GitHub ↗</a><a href={profile.linkedin}>LinkedIn ↗</a></div></div><div class="resume-actions"><button class="button" id="print-resume" hidden>Print / Save as PDF ↗</button><a class="text-link" href="/resume.pdf" download="Akaash_Bella_Resume.pdf">Download resume PDF ↓</a><span class="caption">Original resume; phone number redacted.</span></div></header>
    <section><h2>Education</h2><div class="resume-school"><h3>Oregon State University <span>Corvallis, Oregon</span></h3>{education.map(item=><div class="resume-line"><span>{item.degree}</span><span>{item.date}</span></div>)}<p>Double bachelor’s degree · September 2021–December 2025 · Minor in Business</p></div></section>
    <section><h2>Technical skills</h2><dl class="resume-skills">{skills.map(skill=><div><dt>{skill.title}</dt><dd>{skill.items}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
    <section><h2>Research experience</h2><div class="resume-position"><div class="resume-line"><h3>{experience[0].title} · Oregon State University</h3><span>{experience[0].period}</span></div><p class="position-subtitle">Weight Perturbation Sensitivity in Convolutional Neural Network Training</p><ul>{experience[0].points.map(point=><li>{point}</li>)}<li>Use NumPy, pandas, and Matplotlib for experiment-metric processing and visualization infrastructure.</li></ul></div></section>
    <section><h2>Academic & project experience</h2><div class="resume-position"><div class="resume-line"><h3>{experience[1].title} · Oregon State University</h3><span>{experience[1].period}</span></div><ul>{experience[1].points.map(point=><li>{point}</li>)}</ul></div>
      <div class="resume-position"><div class="resume-line"><h3><a href="/work/researchseek/">ResearchSeek · Independent technical project</a></h3><span>October 2026–present</span></div><ul><li>Developing a local-first CLI search architecture using Python, C++17, pybind11, and SQLite/FTS5.</li><li>Stage 1 foundation includes package setup, CLI surface, an FTS5 probe, and a native build diagnostic. Embeddings, cosine top-k retrieval, incremental indexing, and benchmarks remain planned in the current repository.</li></ul></div>
      <div class="resume-position"><div class="resume-line"><h3><a href="/work/agbizlogic/">Capstone Project Lead · AgBizLogic</a></h3><span>2024–2025</span></div><ul><li>Led a cross-functional team over three terms to develop and manage an AI Wizard-of-Oz prototype for grower decision-support tools.</li><li>The team used iterative usability and trust evaluation to deliver a strategic product roadmap and UX recommendations to AgBizLogic stakeholders.</li></ul></div>
      <div class="resume-position"><div class="resume-line"><h3><a href="/work/mauka-energy/">Consulting Project · Mauka Energy (FEVER/BEVER)</a></h3><span>2025</span></div><ul><li>Developed a commercialization strategy for regenerative braking and routing tools, integrating technical information with market-demand analysis.</li><li>Contributed financial models, including NPV and payback-period analysis, and strategic recommendations for leadership. Financial projections are scenarios, not realized outcomes.</li></ul></div>
    </section>
    <section><h2>Relevant coursework</h2>{coursework.map(group=><p><strong>{group.title}:</strong> {group.courses}</p>)}</section>
    <section><h2>Awards</h2><ul><li>Dean’s List, six-time recipient · Oregon State University</li><li>State Retail Champion · Oregon DECA State Career Development Conference, Sunset High School</li></ul></section>
    <p class="caption resume-source">Education and professional history follow the owner-supplied resume, reviewed October 22, 2026. Only the phone-redacted PDF is published. ResearchSeek and research implementation status follow current public project documentation where it differs from the PDF.</p>
  </article>
  <script>const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#print-resume'); if (button) { button.hidden = false; button.addEventListener('click', () => window.print()); }</script>
</Layout>
